{
  "description": "Golden vectors for the canonical encoding. Each case pairs an input (a parsed JSON object) with the exact canonical bytes (hex-encoded) the encoder must produce. The hex is authored by hand against RFC 8259, independent of the Python implementation, so a stranger in another language can verify byte-compatibility without reading this code. Floats are not permitted (see schema/README.md), so no float case appears.",
